    "q-265746": {
      "dom_id": "step-q265746",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(x,w)=3{w}^{T}x-‖w{‖}^{2}+1\n$$\n\nthat maps two vectors to a scalar, find ${∇}_{w}f.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the results \n\n$$\n{∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)=x,\\,{∇}_{w}({w}^{T}w)=2w,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}(3{w}^{T}x-‖w{‖}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)-{∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}^{2})+{∇}_{w}(1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)-{∇}_{w}({w}^{T}w)+{∇}_{w}(1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot x-2w+0 \\\\  & =3x-2w.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
